.TH STAT 1
.SH NAME
stat \- details of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stat
.IR path ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stat
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
For each
.I path
it prints its object number on the disk, type and permissions, size in
bytes and in blocks, number of links, owner and group numbers, and three
times (UTC): last modified, last changed, created. A symbolic link is
described itself, not what it points to.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 at the first path that cannot be read.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ls (1),
.BR df (1),
.BR sh (1)
